I have everything needed. Here is the complete picture of how owner creation works.

## 1. The POST /owners endpoint YAML

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`**
```yaml
composition:
  authorize: "hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')"

validate:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.ValidateOwnerFields
  next: checkTelephoneUnique

checkTelephoneUnique:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: build

build:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.BuildOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: save

save:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.SaveOwner
  govern: [ transaction ]
  next: respond

respond:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.function.owner.RespondWithOwnerCreated
  govern: [ transaction ]
```
The actual URL is `POST /api/owners` (the file lives under `rest/api/`). Guarded by `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')`.

## 2. Function classes in the pipeline

All under `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`

- **ValidateOwnerFields.java** — first step. Reads `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, checks required fields, normalizes telephone to 10 digits, normalizes email, publishes `Out<OwnerFieldsDto> validated`. Throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException`, `InvalidOwnerEmailException`.
- **CheckOwnerTelephoneUnique.java** — reads `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, scans `ownerRepository.findAll()`, throws `DuplicateTelephoneException` on collision.
- **BuildOwner.java** — reads `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, maps to entity via `ownerMapper.toOwner(request)`, publishes `Out<Owner> built`.
- **SaveOwner.java** — reads `@Val Owner`, calls `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.
- **RespondWithOwnerCreated.java** — reads `@Val Owner`, maps via `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, sends `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}` and an `OwnerDto` body.

Their full source is in the earlier reads (each is a single `service(...)` method). The GET responder used by the displayName test is **RespondWithOwner.java** (same dir):
```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerMapper ownerMapper, ObjectResponse<OwnerDto> response) {
    response.send(ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner));
}
```

## 3. Owner entity + getters

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** — `@Entity` extending `Person`. Own fields: `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`, `Set<Pet> pets`, with standard getters/setters.

`firstName`/`lastName` live on the superclass **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Person.java`**:
```java
@MappedSuperclass
public class Person extends BaseEntity {
    @Column(name = "first_name") @NotEmpty protected String firstName;
    @Column(name = "last_name")  @NotEmpty protected String lastName;
    public String getFirstName() { return this.firstName; }
    public void setFirstName(String firstName) { this.firstName = firstName; }
    public String getLastName() { return this.lastName; }
    public void setLastName(String lastName) { this.lastName = lastName; }
}
```

## 4. The response DTO — important finding

There is **no hand-written `OwnerResponse` / `OwnerDto` class and no `from(...)` factory**. `OwnerDto` and `OwnerFieldsDto` are **generated at build time by the openapi-generator-maven-plugin** from the OpenAPI spec, and the entity↔DTO conversion is done by **MapStruct** (`OwnerMapper`), not a factory method.

- Generator config: `/home/daniel/sandbox/pom.xml` (plugin `org.openapitools:openapi-generator-maven-plugin` 7.23.0), `inputSpec = src/main/resources/openapi.yml`, `modelPackage = org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.dto`, output `target/generated-sources/openapi/...` (not yet generated — the target dir is absent, so no `.java` exists yet).
- Mapper: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** — `@Mapper` interface with `OwnerDto toOwnerDto(Owner)`, `Owner toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` (ignores `id`, `pets`), etc.
- Schema source: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`**:
  - `OwnerFields` (→ `OwnerFieldsDto`, request body) at **line 1991**: properties `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone`, `email`; required: firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.
  - `Owner` (→ `OwnerDto`, response) at **line 2046**: `allOf` OwnerFields plus `id` (readOnly) and `pets` (readOnly array). **No `displayName` field exists.**

To add a `displayName` to the create/GET response you would: add the property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, and populate it in `OwnerMapper` (e.g. a default/`@Mapping` expression building `lastName + ", " + firstName`) — since there is no factory method to edit.

## 5. Tests for owner creation + displayName

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/Cp05Tests.java`** — the displayName test:
```java
@Tag("cp05")
class Cp05Tests extends AcceptanceBase {
    @Test
    void coreComputesDisplayName() throws Exception {
        ObjectNode o = ownerNode();
        o.put("firstName", "John");
        String last = o.get("lastName").asText();
        int id = createOwnerOk(o);
        getOwner(id).andExpect(jsonPath("$.displayName").value(last + ", John"));
    }
}
```
It creates an owner via `POST /api/owners` then GETs it and asserts `$.displayName == "LastName, John"`. This currently has no backing field, so it will fail until `displayName` is added.

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the shared black-box harness (full source read above). Key helpers: `ownerNode()` builds a valid unique owner payload; `createOwner`/`createOwnerOk` POST to `/api/owners`; `getOwner(id)` GETs `/api/owners/{id}`; `extractId` reads `id` from body or the `Location` header. Runs `@SpringBootTest @AutoConfigureMockMvc @Transactional @WithMockUser(roles OWNER_ADMIN, VET_ADMIN, ADMIN)`.

`displayName` appears nowhere in `src/main` — only in the test. No other POST-to-/owners tests exist.

